# Context Orchestration Engine - worker credentials
#
# Each worker in config/workers.json names the env var it reads via
# "api_key_env". Nothing else in the system knows which provider is behind it.
#
# Copy this file to .env and fill in the workers you actually want to run:
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# Any worker without a resolvable key makes `python main.py run` fall back to
# the offline mock gateway. Pass --real to force live calls.

WORKER_1_API_KEY=
WORKER_2_API_KEY=
WORKER_3_API_KEY=
WORKER_4_API_KEY=
WORKER_5_API_KEY=

# Several workers may share one key - point them at the same env var in
# config/workers.json, or reuse the same value here.
#
# Example: run all five workers on one provider by setting every worker's
# "model" to that provider's model string and every "api_key_env" to
# WORKER_1_API_KEY.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Lending keys to visitors
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# The playground can offer a visitor a key rather than asking for one, so a
# first run needs no account anywhere. The keys stay on the server: the page is
# told how many there are and which vendor issued them, and nothing else.
#
# With nothing set below, the WORKER_n_API_KEY values above are the pool, one
# dealt to each worker in turn. To use a different set, list them here:
#
# COE_DEMO_KEYS=gsk_aaa,gsk_bbb,gsk_ccc
#
# Only put free-tier keys here on a public deployment. Anyone who can reach the
# page can spend them, and a run costs real quota.
#
# COE_NO_POOL=1      Lend nothing. Every visitor brings their own key.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deployment flags (see docs/DEPLOYMENT.md). Leave these unset locally.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# COE_SERVERLESS=1   The playground starts and streams a run in one request.
#                    vercel.json sets this.
# COE_ALLOW_LIVE=1   Allow real model calls on a serverless deployment that
#                    has no pool of its own to lend.
# COE_NO_LIVE=1      Refuse real model calls entirely. The stand-in still runs
#                    the whole engine offline.
# COE_GATEWAY=litellm
#                    Route real calls through LiteLLM instead of the built-in
#                    HTTP gateway. Wider provider coverage, and a much larger
#                    install. The HTTP gateway is the default and needs nothing.
# COE_DB=/tmp/playground.db
#                    Where the deployed app writes SQLite.
